# Campaigns Module: Complete API Reference & Report

The Campaign module backend has been completely overhauled to support the rich, dynamic UI features described in your mockups. Every gap has been filled—from the ledger and analytics to WhatsApp template generation and Excel exports.

Here is a full report of what was implemented and how the frontend should use the new endpoints.

---

## 1. Core Schema & Settings Updates

The most critical architectural change was defining the `CampaignSettings` schema and mapping it to the Postgres `settings_override` JSON column.

- **Data Safety:** The frontend now receives a `settings` object inside every `CampaignOut` response.
- **Aliases Fixed:** Pydantic now properly outputs `id` instead of `campaign_id`, preventing the frontend from breaking when parsing lists.
- **Default Injection:** When a campaign is created via `POST /groups/{group_id}/campaigns`, the backend automatically generates a secure 4-digit `access_pin` and default templates (like `paid_indicator: "✔"`).

